---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Perrine",
  servesCuisine: ["American", "Contemporary"],
  priceRange: "$$$",
  telephone: "+1-212-940-8195",
  url: "https://www.perrinenyc.com",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "2 E 61st St",
    addressLocality: "New York",
    addressRegion: "NY",
    postalCode: "10065",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "The Pierre hotel's all-day restaurant on the Upper East Side — breakfast, lunch, and afternoon tea with French-American cooking and Indian touches.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Perrine Menu Guide — The Pierre, Prices & Tea"
  description="Independent guide to Perrine at The Pierre hotel: breakfast, lunch and afternoon tea ($125–$210) with reported prices, what to order, and visiting tips. Prices reported as of October 2026."
  path="/perrine-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/perrine.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/perrine.webp"
      alt="Illustration of an elegant hotel afternoon tea with a tiered stand of sandwiches and pastries — an artist's interpretation, not the actual Perrine"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Upper East Side · The Pierre
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Perrine — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      At 2 East 61st Street, The Pierre's all-day restaurant does something the grander hotel rooms
      don't: it feeds you from morning to afternoon without ceremony. Breakfast is a serious affair,
      lunch is crisp French-American cooking, and the afternoon tea is one of the Upper East Side's
      best-kept rituals. Chef Ashfer Biju's menu carries quiet Indian touches — a masala omelet, a
      coronation chicken salad, a mango lassi — that set it apart from every other hotel dining room
      in the neighborhood. Below is our independent walkthrough with reported prices, plus what we'd
      order. Everything is written in our own words; prices are reported figures, not a copy of the menu.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">2 E 61st St, New York, NY 10065 (inside The Pierre)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">French-American with Indian touches; serious breakfast</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Breakfast/lunch reported $23–72; afternoon tea $125–$210</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Afternoon tea</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Reported from $125/person; seatings vary — confirm when booking</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Recommended, especially for tea; book via Resy</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Phone</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">+1 (212) 940-8195</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Breakfast</h2>
      <p>
        This is Perrine's strongest service — a full, classic hotel breakfast menu reported from
        <strong>$25 to $36</strong>, with the Pierre's own twists. The masala omelet and the corned
        beef hash are the two dishes you won't find done this well elsewhere on the block.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Dish</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Reported price</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Steak &amp; eggs — 6oz NY strip, fried eggs, hash browns</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$36</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Corned beef hash — classic Pierre recipe, twin poached eggs</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$31</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Bagel &amp; lox — Catskills smoked salmon, condiments</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$29</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Eggs Benedict — Canadian bacon or smoked salmon</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$29</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Avocado toast with twin fried eggs and crispy capers</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$29</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Ham &amp; cheese omelet — French ham, Swiss</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$29</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Masala omelet — rolled Indian omelet, tomato, cilantro, green chilies</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$28</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Egg white omelet with spinach, tomato, asparagus</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$28</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Fried egg rancheros with spicy tomato coulis, avocado</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$28</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Ancient grains &amp; eggs with mushrooms, kale, poached egg</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$26</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Brioche French toast — cinnamon sugar, strawberry compote</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$25</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">The Pierre Bloody Mary</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$18</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Mimosa</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$16</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">White peach bellini</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$15</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Lunch — salads, pasta &amp; mains</h2>
      <p>
        Lunch salads run <strong>$24–44</strong>, pastas and flatbreads <strong>$23–34</strong>, and
        mains <strong>$29–72</strong>. The coronation chicken — a curry chicken salad created for
        Queen Elizabeth II's coronation in the 1950s — is the house legend.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Dish</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Reported price</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Maine lobster salad — endives, radishes, green apple rémoulade</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$44</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Black sea bass — seafood broth, fava beans, fines herbes</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$38</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Cavatelli with chicken sausage, scallions, white wine</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$34</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Roasted salmon — beluga lentils, gribiche, sorrel sauce</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$34</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Seared tuna salad — kale, barley, pomegranate, poached egg</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$32</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Linguine with white clam sauce, lemon, serrano chilies</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$32</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Rainbow chard &amp; goat cheese tart</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$31</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Chicken paillard — arugula, artichokes, lemon vinaigrette</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$31</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">The Pierre burger — grass-fed beef, rémoulade, Rupert cheese, frites</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$29</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Grilled shrimp salad — avocado, spiced lemon aïoli</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$29</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Upstate farms roasted vegetables with barley and feta</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$29</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Coronation chicken — curry chicken salad, raisins, herbs, country bread</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$24</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Zucchini blossom flatbread on house-made naan</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$23</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Steak frites with watercress salad</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$49</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Dover sole, sauce meunière</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$72</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Sides run <strong>$9–12</strong> (pommes frites, glazed carrots, spiced cauliflower, charred
        broccoli gratin), and there's a mango lassi at $9 — the Indian touch extends to the drinks.
      </p>

      <h2>Afternoon tea</h2>
      <p>
        Perrine's tea service is the sleeper hit of this list. Reported tiers: <strong>Traditional
        Afternoon Tea at $125 per person</strong>, the <strong>Pierre Afternoon Tea at $160</strong>
        (adds champagne and Russian ossetra caviar), and the <strong>Golden Caviar Afternoon Tea at
        $210</strong> (two glasses of champagne or a demi bottle plus golden ossetra), with a
        <strong>$75 menu for younger guests</strong>. Expect tea sandwiches, cranberry scones with
        Devonshire cream, and pastries from the hotel's pâtissiers. Reported service windows have
        varied (11am–4pm in some listings; fixed seatings in others) — confirm the current schedule
        when you book.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Breakfast:</strong> the masala omelet — it's the one dish no other hotel room on this list serves.</li>
        <li><strong>Lunch:</strong> the coronation chicken. History you can eat, at $24.</li>
        <li><strong>The splurge:</strong> afternoon tea at the $160 tier — champagne and caviar in The Pierre is the full experience.</li>
        <li><strong>The burger test:</strong> the Pierre burger is the benchmark for hotel burgers on the Upper East Side.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Tea needs a reservation</strong> — book on Resy and confirm the seating times, which have varied.</li>
        <li><strong>Breakfast is walk-in friendly</strong> compared to the grander rooms — a good low-commitment first visit.</li>
        <li><strong>Dress code is polished-casual;</strong> it's The Pierre, but Perrine is the relaxed sibling.</li>
        <li><strong>Pair it with Central Park</strong> — the hotel sits two blocks from the park's southeast corner, perfect for a post-lunch walk.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        Prices above are <strong>reported as of October 2026</strong>, compiled from publicly reported
        menus and listings. Menus change seasonally and prices move — tea service times and tiers in
        particular should be confirmed at booking. Always verify current prices with the restaurant
        before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
